From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kiritantakechi <kiritantakechi@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 23:55:25 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] uboot-rockchip: build in the A/B slot logic of wrt-build's
 boards

Include wrt-build's A/B glue, env/uboot/wrt-ab.mk, after the variants'
definitions. When the variant being built is one of the boards listed in
env/wrt-boards.mk, the glue adds the configuration fragments wrt-ab.config
and board-<id>.config after its defconfig, and prepares its default
environment: the board's constants followed by the shared slot logic. The
stored environment may set only boot_slot, bootcount and
upgrade_available (ENV_WRITEABLE_LIST). Every other variant is unchanged.
---
 package/boot/uboot-rockchip/Makefile | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/package/boot/uboot-rockchip/Makefile b/package/boot/uboot-rockchip/Makefile
index 7161e56..8b38de5 100644
--- a/package/boot/uboot-rockchip/Makefile
+++ b/package/boot/uboot-rockchip/Makefile
@@ -514,4 +514,8 @@ endef
 define Package/u-boot/install/default
 endef
 
+# The A/B slot logic of wrt-build for the U-Boot variants of its boards
+# (env/wrt-boards.mk), whose definitions above env/uboot/wrt-ab.mk extends.
+include $(TOPDIR)/env/uboot/wrt-ab.mk
+
 $(eval $(call BuildPackage/U-Boot))
